# Fail-closed build context for docker/backend.Dockerfile.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit only what the image build actually reads.
# Rationale: this repo's build context used to be ~358 MB (venv, node_modules,
# model weights, graphify-out). An allowlist means a newly added secret — .env,
# a stray *.pem, an export dump — cannot leak into the image just because
# someone forgot to extend an exclusion list. New file? Add it here on purpose.
#
# Measured effect: 357.8 MB -> 374.8 kB.
#
# !! FORMAT GOTCHA — READ BEFORE EDITING !!
# .dockerignore has NO inline comments. A pattern line may not carry a trailing
# `# ...`, and it does not use the Dockerfile's line-continuation backslash.
# Writing:
#     !pyproject.toml    # tool config
# makes the ENTIRE line one literal pattern ("!pyproject.toml    # tool config"),
# which matches nothing — so the file is silently excluded and the build fails
# later with a confusing "not found" on the COPY, not here. Put every comment on
# its own line above the pattern. This actually bit this repo once already.

**

# --- admitted: build inputs -------------------------------------------------
!requirements.txt
# Tool config, copied into the image for parity with local runs.
!pyproject.toml
!backend/**

# --- excluded even inside admitted dirs ------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*

# NOTE: requirements-dev.txt is deliberately NOT admitted. It is dev-only
# tooling (pytest/ruff/mypy); admitting it would put the test runner in the
# production image. Local + CI install it directly, outside the image build.